WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.800
In 1973 and 1974, the world
price of oil roughly quadrupled.

2
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.370
Over 1974, US consumer
prices rose 12.3 percent.

3
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:17.580
And by May 1975, unemployment
had reached 9 percent.

4
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.580
Usually, when spending booms, prices
climb and more people find work.

5
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:26.300
So why did prices and
unemployment climb together?

6
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.890
In this mission, you'll find
short-run and long-run equilibrium

7
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.590
on the aggregate demand and supply graph.

8
00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:35.570
Then you'll shock the
economy in two graph labs

9
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.830
and predict what happens
to the price level,

10
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.130
real GDP, and jobs.

11
00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:43.680
Your mission: find out why
prices and unemployment can

12
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.240
rise at the same time.
